  "Created in 1987 by merging Louis Vuitton, founded 1854, with Moët Hennessy. Bernard Arnault has controlled and led it since 1989, building the world's largest luxury group. It owns roughly 75 maisons: Louis Vuitton and Dior in fashion and leather goods, which generate most of the profit; Tiffany, Bulgari and TAG Heuer in jewellery and watches; Sephora in selective retail; Moët & Chandon, Dom Pérignon and Hennessy in wines and spirits; and Guerlain and Parfums Christian Dior in perfumes and cosmetics. Prices quoted in euros.",
  [("Fashion & Leather Goods", 49), ("Selective Retailing (Sephora, DFS)", 19), ("Perfumes & Cosmetics", 12), ("Watches & Jewelry", 12), ("Wines & Spirits", 8)],
